From: gts9wifi Ubuntu port
Subject: [PATCH] media: hi1337-gts9u: drop stream-start debug reads and 500 ms sleep

The X710 driver carried bring-up debugging in hi1337_start_streaming():
three register reads after the mode tables, two after stream-on and a
msleep(500) between them, all logged at info level.  Every stream start
took ~0.8 s.  Applications that reconfigure the camera (GNOME Snapshot
opens, reconfigures and restarts within a second) then start the sensor
again while the previous start is still sleeping; on the rear sensor
that ended in a CCI timeout ("master 1 queue 0 timeout", -110 writing
0x0790), a failed STREAMON and an unresponsive camera.

The S9 Ultra version of this driver has no such block.  Behaviour is
otherwise unchanged; the lens binding the X710 version adds is kept.
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hi1337_gts9u.c	2026-10-18 05:08:54.327501182 +0300
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hi1337_gts9u.c	2026-10-18 05:08:54.342662112 +0300
@@ -373,12 +373,8 @@
 static int hi1337_start_streaming(struct hi1337 *sensor)
 {
 	const struct hi1337_mode *mode = &sensor->variant->mode;
-	u16 dbg_val = 0;
 	int ret;
 
-	dev_info(sensor->dev, "DBG: start_streaming %s (%ux%u)\n",
-		 mode->name, mode->width, mode->height);
-
 	ret = hi1337_write_table(sensor, hi1337_global_regs,
 				 ARRAY_SIZE(hi1337_global_regs));
 	if (ret)
@@ -387,17 +383,6 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	/* DBG: confirm what the sensor actually reads back after the tables. */
-	ret = hi1337_read_reg(sensor, HI1337_REG_MODE_SELECT, &dbg_val);
-	dev_info(sensor->dev, "DBG: after tables MODE_SELECT=0x%04x (r=%d)\n",
-		 dbg_val, ret);
-	ret = hi1337_read_reg(sensor, HI1337_REG_MODEL_ID, &dbg_val);
-	dev_info(sensor->dev, "DBG: after tables MODEL_ID=0x%04x (r=%d)\n",
-		 dbg_val, ret);
-	ret = hi1337_read_reg(sensor, HI1337_REG_FRAME_LENGTH, &dbg_val);
-	dev_info(sensor->dev, "DBG: after tables FRAME_LENGTH=0x%04x (r=%d)\n",
-		 dbg_val, ret);
-
 	sensor->streaming = true;
 	ret = __v4l2_ctrl_handler_setup(&sensor->ctrl_handler);
 	if (ret)
@@ -406,15 +391,6 @@
 			       HI1337_MODE_STREAMING);
 	if (ret)
 		goto clear_streaming;
-
-	/* DBG: prove the stream-on write stuck. */
-	ret = hi1337_read_reg(sensor, HI1337_REG_MODE_SELECT, &dbg_val);
-	dev_info(sensor->dev, "DBG: after stream-on MODE_SELECT=0x%04x (r=%d)\n",
-		 dbg_val, ret);
-	msleep(500);
-	ret = hi1337_read_reg(sensor, HI1337_REG_MODE_SELECT, &dbg_val);
-	dev_info(sensor->dev, "DBG: 500ms later MODE_SELECT=0x%04x (r=%d)\n",
-		 dbg_val, ret);
 	return 0;
 
 clear_streaming:
